{"type": "sena", "labs": [{"stimuli": [{"template_override": 1, "type": "welcome", "_data": [], "contents": [{}], "id": 0}, {"template_override": 1, "_data": [], "type": "audio", "title": "", "contents": [{"type": "slideshow", "value": {"audiosrc": "engenn9le17ob10re2aud01", "coverimg": "engenn9le17ob10re2img01.jpg", "images": [{"image": "engenn9le17ob10re2img02.jpg", "text": "", "time": "0", "id": 0}, {"image": "engenn9le17ob10re2img02.jpg", "text": "If an actor finds one thing difficult, it's getting a job. Traditionally, this has happened through an audition. An audition has given a director the chance to see what the actor can do. Perhaps the actor prepared a monologue or speech from a play and presented this to the director. Maybe the director has given the actor a scene from the play that he or she wanted to cast.", "time": "100", "id": 1}, {"image": "engenn9le17ob10re2img01.jpg", "text": "The actor could also do a cold reading. In a cold reading the director has handed the actor an unfamiliar scene. When they really want to see someone that's they way to do it. If you're wonderful, it's the way to land the part. When you're not, it's try again later.<br /><br />Sometimes, a director is putting together a company.  If the actors work together, they become an ensemble. When that's the case, the director often asks the actors to do improvisations.", "time": "22500", "id": 2}, {"image": "engenn9le17ob10re2img03.jpg", "text": "When an improvisation starts, and the actors have gotten into character, the director might suggest things like: \"Don't you think you should reverse roles?\" \"You wouldn't really want to forgive her, would you?\" \"Couldn't you do it again and make different choices?\" The actors then have to decide for themselves: \"Sure I can\", or \"No, I wouldn't\", or \"Yes, I think I could.\"<br /><br />Many actors have learned this way. Emma Watson did improvisations with the cast when she was on Broadway. It helped her understand that she was part of a solid unit that knew each other well. It has, she says, made all the difference to how she feels on stage.", "time": "50000", "id": 3}]}}], "id": 1}], "exercises": [{"template_override": 1, "type": "WLC", "img_path": "", "questions": [], "_data": [{"type": "instructions", "contents": [{"content": " I can talk about work and entertainment.", "type": "Learning Outcomes"}, {"content": " I can talk about emotions and reactions in different situations. ", "type": "Learning Outcomes"}, {"content": " I can make and respond to suggestions. ", "type": "Learning Outcomes"}, {"content": "Do you think an acting class might be valuable to people other than actors? How?", "type": "Free Header Item"}, {"content": " Would you consider taking an acting class?  Why or why not?", "type": "Free Header Item"}]}, {"type": "group", "contents": [{"content": "Welcome", "type": "group_name"}]}, {"content": {"allowed_attempts": 2, "incorrect_feedback": [{"content": "try again", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Maybe next time", "type": "text"}], "correct_feedback": "Correct", "attempt_feedback": [{"content": "You have 2 tries", "type": "text"}, {"content": "you have 1 attempt left", "type": "text"}]}, "type": "feedback"}, {"content": "Ask your partner:", "type": "free_header_text"}, {"content": "Let's take an acting class!", "type": "free_type_text_area"}], "id": 0, "stimuli_ids": [0]}, {"template_override": 1, "type": "STI", "questions": [{"responses": [{"_data": [{"content": "", "type": "text"}], "id": 0, "correct": 0, "selected": 0}, {"_data": [{"content": "", "type": "text"}], "id": 1, "correct": 1, "selected": 0}], "_data": [{"type": "question", "contents": [{"content": "", "type": "text"}]}], "id": 0}], "_data": [{"type": "instructions", "contents": [{"content": "<span class=\"tool-tip\" id=\"tip_1_0\"> Emma Watson</span> did improvisations with the cast when she was on Broadway!", "type": "text"}]}, {"type": "group", "contents": [{"content": "Content", "type": "group_name"}]}, {"cont