ity expressions, grammar, and coherence and cohesion aspects appropriate for this level. ", "type": "secondary_2"}, {"content": " Writes effective texts in English showing good organization and appropriate use of language to create the intended effect for the purpose and context.  Writes well organized texts through the correct use of formality expressions, grammar, and coherence and cohesion aspects appropriate for this level. ", "type": "secondary_3"}, {"content": " Writes effective texts in English showing good organization and appropriate use of language to create the intended effect for the purpose and context.  Writes well organized texts through the correct use of formality expressions, grammar, and coherence and cohesion aspects appropriate for this level. ", "type": "secondary_4"}, {"content": " Writes effective texts in English showing good organization and appropriate use of language to create the intended effect for the purpose and context.  Writes well organized texts through the correct use of formality expressions, grammar, and coherence and cohesion aspects appropriate for this level. ", "type": "secondary_5"}, {"content": " Writes effective texts in English showing good organization and appropriate use of language to create the intended effect for the purpose and context.  Writes well organized texts through the correct use of formality expressions, grammar, and coherence and cohesion aspects appropriate for this level. ", "type": "secondary_6"}, {"content": " Writes effective texts in English showing good organization and appropriate use of language to create the intended effect for the purpose and context.  Writes well organized texts through the correct use of formality expressions, grammar, and coherence and cohesion aspects appropriate for this level. ", "type": "secondary_7"}, {"content": " Writes effective texts in English showing good organization and appropriate use of language to create the intended effect for the purpose and context.  Writes well organized texts through the correct use of formality expressions, grammar, and coherence and cohesion aspects appropriate for this level. ", "type": "secondary_8"}]}, {"content": "engenn9le17ob10re1img01.jpg", "type": "background_image"}, {"type": "learning_points", "contents": [{"content": " Making and Responding to Suggestions", "type": "heading"}, {"content": " You can use <span class=\"strong\">modals</span> or the <span class=\"strong\">zero conditional</span> to make suggestions. ", "type": "describer"}, {"content": "Common phrases with <span class=\"strong\">modals</span> you use to make suggestions are:", "type": "text"}, {"content": "<span class=\"italic\">Do you think you should ...?<br/> You could ...<br/> You should ... <br/> Couldn't you ...?</span> ", "type": "text"}, {"content": "You can also use the <span class=\"strong\">zero conditional</span> to make suggestions in a more indirect way. ", "type": "text"}, {"content": "For example:", "type": "text"}, {"content": "<span class=\"italic\">If you're wonderful, it's the way to land the part. </span> ", "type": "text"}, {"content": "The structure of the <span class=\"strong\">zero conditional</span> is:", "type": "text"}, {"content": "If + <span class=\"strong\">Simple Present</span>, <span class=\"strong\">Simple Present</span>", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Don't you think you should reverse roles? ", "type": "example"}, {"content": "Couldn't you do it again and make different choices?", "type": "example"}, {"content": "If you're wonderful, it's the way to land the part. ", "type": "example"}, {"content": "When you're not, it's try again later.", "type": "example"}]}, {"type": "learning_points", "contents": [{"content": " The Present Perfect Tense vs. The Simple Past Tense", "type": "heading"}, {"content": "You use the <span class=\"strong\">Present Perfect tense</span> to talk about a past action or an action that began in the past that is connected to the present in some way. <br/> You use the <span class=\"strong\">Simple Past tense</span> to talk about many kinds of past events: short, quickly finished actions, longer situations and repeated events. ", "type": "describer"}, {"content": "You can use the <span class=\"strong\">Present Perfect tense </span> to talk about experience.<br/> When you use the <span class=\"strong\">Present Perfect tense</span>, you think about the past and present together. There is some connection between what happened in the past and now.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "For example: ", "type": "text"}, {"content": "<span class=\"italic\">I have learned English.</span>  = I learned English in the past and now I can speak English.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "<span class=\"italic\">He has bought a painting.</span>  = He bought the painting in the past and now he has a painting.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Usually, when you use the <span class=\"strong\">Simple Past tense</span> , the time of the finished action is clear from the context or explicitly mentioned in the sentence.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "For example:", "type": "text"}, {"content": "<span class=\"italic\"><span class=\"strong\">Yesterday</span> , I <span class=\"strong\">went </span> to the store.<br/>   Emma Watson <span class=\"strong\">did </span> improvisations with the cast <span class=\"strong\">when </span> she was on Broadway. </span> ", "type": "text"}, {"content": "It is clear when the action occurred. In this sentence we would not use the <span class=\"strong\">Present Perfect</span> <span class=\"italic\">(<strike>Yesterday, I have been to the store</strike>).</span> ", "type": "text"}, {"content": "The audition has given the director the chance to see what the actor can do. ", "type": "example"}, {"content": "Perhaps the actor has prepared a monologue or speech from a play and presented this to the director. ", "type": "example"}, {"content": "Maybe the director has given the actor a scene from the play that he or she wanted to cast.  ", "type": "example"}, {"content": "The director has handed the actor an unfamiliar scene.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "The actors have gotten into character, so the director may call out suggestions.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "Many actors have learned this way. ", "type": "example"}, {"content": "Emma Watson did improvisations with the cast when she was on Broadway. ", "type": "example"}, {"content": "It helped her understand that she was part of a solid unit that knew each other well. ", "type": "example"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "traditionally", "type": "name"}, {"content": "\u200baccording to \u200btradition; in a \u200btraditional way", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(adverb)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: Traditionally, this has happened through an audition.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn9le17ob10aud01", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word_describer", "contents": [{"content": " These are words you use when you talk about acting.", "type": "text"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "monologue", "type": "name"}, {"content": "a \u200blong \u200bspeech by one \u200bperson", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(noun)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: Perhaps the actor prepared a monologue or speech from a play.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn9le17ob10aud02", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "to present", "type": "name"}, {"content": "to give, \u200bprovide, or make something \u200bknown", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(verb)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: The actor presented his monologue to the director.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn9le17ob10aud03", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "scene", "type": "name"}, {"content": "a \u200bpart of a \u200bplay or \u200bfilm in which the \u200baction \u200bstays in one \u200bplace for a \u200bperiod of \u200btime", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(noun)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: The director has handed the actor an unfamiliar scene. ", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn9le17ob10aud04", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "cold reading", "type": "name"}, {"content": "reading an unfamiliar line, monologue or part of a text without any practice", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(noun)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: The actor could also do a cold reading.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn9le17ob10aud05", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "to cast", "type": "name"}, {"content": "to \u200bchoose \u200bactors to \u200bplay \u200bparticular \u200bparts in a \u200bplay, \u200bfilm, or show", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(verb)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: Maybe the director has given the actor a scene from the play that he or she wanted to cast.  ", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn9le17ob10aud06", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "unfamiliar", "type": "name"}, {"content": "not having any \u200bknowledge or \u200bexperience of something", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(adjective)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: The director handed the actor an unfamiliar scene to read. ", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn9le17ob10aud07", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "to land (a part)", "type": "name"}, {"content": "to be successful in getting the part you tried out for", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(verb)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example:  If you're wonderful, it's the way to land the part. ", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn9le17ob10aud08", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "improvisation", "type": "name"}, {"content": "a \u200bperformance that an \u200bactor, \u200bmusician, etc. has not \u200bpracticed or \u200bplanned", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(noun)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example:  Emma Watson did improvisation with the cast when she was on Broadway.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn9le17ob10aud09", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "to get into character", "type": "name"}, {"content": "when an actor puts themselves into the role of the person they are portraying", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(expression)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: All the actors have gotten into character.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn9le17ob10aud10", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "takeaway_extension", "contents": [{"content": "Find a short monologue from a modern English play online or at the library.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Make a copy of the monologue and highlight words and phrases that are difficult, then look them up.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Underline words you think should be stressed.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Practice saying the monologue aloud.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Present it to a partner or a group.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Explain the background of the monologue. Who is the character? What is the situation?", "type": "text"}]}, {"type": "takeaway_assessment", "contents": [{"content": "I find a short English monologue.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "I look up new words. ", "type": "text"}, {"content": "I practice saying the monologue aloud,  stressing important words.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "I present the monologue to a partner or a group.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "I explain the background of the monologue.", "type": "text"}]}]}